> Count all six ideal choices, then all twenty-seven choices of a biased model

For three labels, the Fisher–Yates choices are j_2∈{0,1,2} and j_1∈{0,1}; all six
sequences give different outputs. The explicit-choice API can apply a given validated
sequence without a generator. The complete census enumerates that same native swap
kernel, so its six outputs can be checked against ordinary permutation enumeration.

For comparison, define a specific naive model: visit i=0,1,2 in ascending order and
independently choose each j from {0,1,2}. That is 3³=27 equally weighted choice sequences.
They cannot split equally among 3!=6 permutations. This counting obstruction proves
bias for this model; it does not identify every possible flawed shuffle.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fy_choices.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
const auto good=dm::algorithms::shuffle_choice_census(3);
  const auto bad=dm::algorithms::shuffle_choice_census(3,dm::algorithms::ShuffleCensusRule::AllPositions);
  const auto explicit_output=dm::algorithms::fisher_yates_from_choices({1,2,3},{0,0});
  std::print("Explicit choices (0,0) produce {} {} {}.\n\n",explicit_output[0],explicit_output[1],explicit_output[2]);
  std::print("| output ordering | shrinking-tree count / 6 | full-range count / 27 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::vector<double>x,a,b;std::size_t rank=0;
  for(const auto&[p,count]:good.permutation_counts){const auto other=bad.permutation_counts.at(p);std::print("| {}{}{} | {} | {} |\n",p[0]+1,p[1]+1,p[2]+1,count,other);x.push_back(++rank);a.push_back(count);b.push_back(other);}
  std::print("\nExact outcomes: shrinking {}; all-positions {}; distinct outputs {} and {}.\n",good.outcomes,bad.outcomes,good.permutation_counts.size(),bad.permutation_counts.size());
  auto left=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();left.bars(x,a,"Count",{37,99,235}).title("Shrinking choices: 6 equally weighted leaves").x_label("Lexicographic ordering rank").y_label("Exact count").x_limits(.4,6.6).y_limits(0,1.4);
  auto right=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();right.bars(x,b,"Count",{220,38,38}).abline_h(27./6,{148,163,184},1.5).title("Full-range choices: counts are 4 or 5").x_label("Same ordering rank").y_label("Exact count").x_limits(.4,6.6).y_limits(0,6);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(left).add(right).size(1100,540).title("Exact choice enumeration, without a random generator").fit_panels().save_svg("build/fy_choices.svg");
}
