> Work, bounded evidence and an actual sampler retry

There are n−1 swap attempts, including self-swaps. A returned-vector API also copies n
values, so its storage is O(n). Trace capture adds an owned input copy and one record
per stage; the complete cap counts C=2n+max(n−1,0) entries before copying or drawing.
The default is one million entries; zero disables only that optional cap. Entry counts
are not bytes, peak memory or runtime. The ordinary and work APIs have no history cap.

Bounded integer draws may consume more than one raw word. For the 64-bit multiply-and-reject
sampler with range size s, the threshold is 2^64 mod s; a product whose low word is below
that threshold is rejected. For the special seed below, the first SplitMix64 word is zero.
At the first three-element stage, s=3 and the threshold is one, so that word is rejected.
The actual shared sampler then accepts a later word. This is an exercised retry, not an
assumption that every stage always consumes one word.

Under independent uniform raw words the acceptance probability is greater than one half,
so expected sampler work is bounded by a constant per stage. There is no deterministic
fixed retry bound in that ideal model. The work counter measures actual retries for a
specified seed; it does not infer speed or statistical independence.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fy_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
constexpr std::uint64_t seed=0x61c8864680b583ebULL;
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::fisher_yates_shuffle_trace({1,2,3},seed,8);
  std::print("| retry-control i | accepted j | raw words consumed |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");for(const auto&s:t.steps)std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",s.i,s.j,s.random_words);
  std::print("\nRetry control: stages {}; raw words {}; output {} {} {}.\n",t.outcome.stages,t.outcome.random_words,t.outcome.values[0],t.outcome.values[1],t.outcome.values[2]);
  bool under=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::fisher_yates_shuffle_trace({1,2,3},seed,7);}catch(const std::length_error&){under=true;}
  bool census_under=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::shuffle_choice_census(3,dm::algorithms::ShuffleCensusRule::FisherYates,32);}catch(const std::length_error&){census_under=true;}
  const auto exact=dm::algorithms::shuffle_choice_census(3,dm::algorithms::ShuffleCensusRule::FisherYates,33);
  auto changed=t;changed.input[0]=99;changed.outcome.values[0]=99;
  std::print("Trace cap 8 succeeds, 7 rejects {}; choice-census cap 33 succeeds, 32 rejects {}; exact outcomes {}.\n",under,census_under,exact.outcomes);
  std::print("Owned copy: original first input {}; original first output {}; edited copy first output {}.\n",t.input[0],t.outcome.values[0],changed.outcome.values[0]);
  std::print("\n| input length | swap attempts | different-position swaps | raw words |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{0,1,3,6,32,1000}){std::vector<int>a(n);std::iota(a.begin(),a.end(),0);const auto r=dm::algorithms::fisher_yates_shuffle_work(a,42);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,r.stages,r.nontrivial_swaps,r.random_words);}
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(60,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle b;b.width=3.8;b.height=1.9;b.font_size=23;
  g.node("first",{0,0},std::format("First stage, i=2\n{} raw words\nOne rejection",t.steps[0].random_words),b).node("last",{5.5,0},std::format("Last stage, i=1\n{} raw word\nNo rejection",t.steps[1].random_words),b).node("result",{11,0},std::format("Total: {} stages\n{} raw words\nOutput: {} {} {}",t.outcome.stages,t.outcome.random_words,t.outcome.values[0],t.outcome.values[1],t.outcome.values[2]),b).edge("first","last").edge("last","result").text({5.5,-2.5},"A bounded-draw call can consume multiple generator words",24).save_svg("build/fy_controls.svg");
  if(!under||!census_under||t.outcome.random_words!=3)throw std::runtime_error("quota or retry check");
}
